---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import pilot from '../../content/pilot.json';
const q=pilot.question;
---
<Base title={q.title}><article class="article" data-pagefind-body><span hidden data-pagefind-filter="discipline:statistics"></span><p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-filter="discipline:climate-science">Q-ENSO-001 / CLIMATE SCIENCE</p><h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{q.title}</h1><p class="lede">A bounded empirical question motivated by an unresolved forecasting problem. No exact answer was located in the documented literature coverage.</p><div class="badges">{Object.entries(q.statuses).map(([dimension,state])=><span class="badge">{dimension}: {state.replaceAll('_',' ')}</span>)}</div><h2>The exact claim</h2><p>{q.scope.claim}</p><p><a class="button" href={'/research/'+pilot.run_id+'/'}>Read the experiment ↗</a></p><h2>Why investigate this?</h2><p>The spring predictability barrier continues to limit ENSO forecasts. This pilot isolates calendar information in a small model before introducing more data or complexity. It does not reproduce the source paper's deep-learning method.</p><blockquote>{q.source_evidence[0].quote}<cite><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2601.02050v1">Gan et al. (2026), abstract, arXiv preprint</a></cite></blockquote><p class="muted">This exact bounded question was formulated by the agent as a follow-up. It is not represented as the authors' verbatim question.</p><h2>Search coverage and related work</h2><p>Five targeted English-language search formulations, source full-text reading, and comparison with relevant 2022–2026 studies. Related work already evaluates seasonal ENSO forecasting; no claim of a new method is made.</p><ul>{q.literature_search.assessed_sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url}>{s.relationship}</a>: {s.finding} <small>Coverage: {s.coverage}</small></li>)}</ul><details><summary>See exact search formulations and limitations</summary><ul>{q.literature_search.queries.map(s=><li>{s}</li>)}</ul><ul>{q.literature_search.limitations.map(s=><li>{s}</li>)}</ul></details><h2>Researchability</h2><p><strong>{q.assessment.score}/100</strong> heuristic readiness score. This expresses whether the bounded computation can be run and checked; it is not a probability of answering the question correctly.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Rating / 4</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(q.assessment.ratings).map(([key,value])=><tr><td>{key.replaceAll('_',' ')}</td><td>{value}</td><td>{typeof q.assessment.evidence[key] === 'string' ? q.assessment.evidence[key] : JSON.stringify(q.assessment.evidence[key])}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><h2>History</h2><p>2026-10-25: source gap assessed, search recorded, internal plan frozen, bounded run completed, fresh reproduction passed. Human scientific review and disclosure approval remain pending. No resolution badge has been assigned.</p><a href="/data/v1/catalog.json">Download question JSON ↗</a></article></Base>
